From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 06:09:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 44/47] Board statistics: keep the track clearance search from
 overflowing

ComputeBoardStatistics() passes the running minimum track-to-track clearance,
initially INT_MAX, to SHAPE::Collide(), which adds half the track width and
the via radius to it. The signed overflow (UBSan in shape_collisions.cpp) made
the clearance negative, so most pairs were not measured and the reported
minimum clearance could be wrong. Cap the search distance. Still present on
master.

Found by tools/bughunt (1000+ boards, pcb export stats).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 pcbnew/board_statistics_report.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pcbnew/board_statistics_report.cpp b/pcbnew/board_statistics_report.cpp
index a0cb2977..ffb8e856 100644
--- a/pcbnew/board_statistics_report.cpp
+++ b/pcbnew/board_statistics_report.cpp
@@ -209,7 +209,10 @@ void ComputeBoardStatistics( BOARD* aBoard, const BOARD_STATISTICS_OPTIONS& aOpt
 
             int  actual = 0;
             auto trackShapeB = otherTrack->GetEffectiveShape( layer );
-            bool collide = trackShapeA->Collide( trackShapeB.get(), aData.minClearanceTrackToTrack, &actual );
+            // The running minimum starts at INT_MAX; the collision code adds half widths and
+            // radii to the clearance, which overflowed and turned "no limit" into a negative one
+            int  clearance = std::min( aData.minClearanceTrackToTrack, std::numeric_limits<int>::max() / 4 );
+            bool collide = trackShapeA->Collide( trackShapeB.get(), clearance, &actual );
 
             if( collide )
                 aData.minClearanceTrackToTrack = std::min( aData.minClearanceTrackToTrack, actual );
